  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Effective measures implemented by constituents to improve integration of sustainable MSMEs into global value chains and promote decent work.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ILO strengthened capacity of key stakeholders in the world of work, the Micro-, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs), through targeted training (SCORE/SCORE4Climate module) to enhance their environmental sustainability, productivity, competitiveness and integration into the circular economy and global value chains. 
Furthermore, ILO provided support in improving the capacity of the National Statistics Committee (NSC) of Kyrgyzstan to produce a Green Jobs Assessment Model (GJAM): a data system and analytical tool to assess the green jobs effects of alternative policies. ILO constituents (the government and social partners) will be supported in their preparations for COP29 (Azerbaijan) and COP30 (Brazil)&#x201d; and benefit from the exchanges with countries at different stages of development.</narrative>
  </description>
